 records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue"],"id":"long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.35 (Greedy survival and membership)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.35, p. 54, label thm:greedy-survival-catalogue","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*With the greedy remainder $r_n(x)$ and complete tail $R_n$,\n$$\nx\\in\\mathcal A\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n x\\ge0\\ \\text{and}\\ r_n(x)\\le R_n\\text{ for every }n\\ge0.\n$$\nIf all inequalities hold, the nonnegative remainders tend to zero because $R_n\\to0$, so the greedy partial sums converge to $x$. Conversely, strict tail domination $w_n>R_n$ forces the greedy choices in any representation and therefore gives every inequality. The argument applies to positive summable weights satisfying that separation hypothesis; it is not a consequence of summability alone.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_greedy_survival%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-greedy-survival-catalogue%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_greedy_survival%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lea